the target language is: lps.

% alice.le — Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, chapters I and II, as a story on
% the library (docs/project/plans/InformPlan.md phase 3). The text is Carroll's, in the
% companion alice.lps; the world is here.
%
% What the story is for: the same choices as the book, or different ones. The
% White Rabbit runs past; Alice follows it down the hole into the hall of
% doors; the golden key is on the glass table and the garden is behind a door
% fifteen inches high. Drink from the bottle and you are small enough for the
% door but the key is out of reach; eat the cake and you are too big for
% anything, and cry a pool; the Rabbit comes back, drops his fan, and fanning
% yourself makes you small again — into the pool you go, and chapter II ends
% swimming. Or take the key first, then drink, and walk into the garden, which
% the book's Alice never does. The Play panel's Fork is the bottle.
%
% Scenario one below is the book's path, checked by tools/if_test.pl;
% alice_garden.le is the other.

the maximum time is 80.

the knowledge base alice includes these resources: world, turns.

the events are:
    the command is to drink *a thing*.
    the command is to eat *a thing*.
    the command is to wave *a thing*.
    *a person* tries to drink *a thing*.
    *a person* tries to eat *a thing*.
    *a person* tries to wave *a thing*.

the actions are:
    *a person* drinks *a thing*; known as drink.
    *a person* eats *a thing*; known as eat.
    *a person* waves *a thing*; known as wave.
    *a person* cannot drink *a thing*.
    *a person* cannot eat *a thing*.
    *a person* cannot wave *a thing*.
    *a person* cries; known as cry.
    *a person* runs from *a room* to *a second room*; known as run.
    *a person* falls into *a room*; known as fall.

the fluents are:
    the size of *a person* is *a size*; known as size.
    the pool of tears exists; known as pool.
    *a person* has cried; known as cried.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is drinkable.
    *a thing* is edible.
    *a thing* is a fan.
    the rabbit runs from *a room* to *a second room*.

the knowledge base alice includes:

% ---- the world

riverbank is a room.
the rabbit hole is a room.
hall is a room.
garden is a room.
the pool of tears is a room.

down from riverbank goes to the rabbit hole.
down from the rabbit hole goes to hall.

the small door is a door.
the small door is openable.
the small door is lockable.
the small door leads south from hall to garden.
the key of the small door is the golden key.

the glass table is a supporter.
the glass table is fixed in place.
bottle is drinkable.
cake is edible.
fan is a fan.

the white rabbit is a person.
sister is a person.
mouse is a person.

the rabbit runs from offstage to riverbank.
the rabbit runs from riverbank to the rabbit hole.
the rabbit runs from the rabbit hole to hall.
the rabbit runs from hall to garden.

initially the turn is 0
    and the first chapter is playing
    and player is in riverbank
    and the size of player is normal
    and sister is in riverbank
    and the white rabbit is in offstage
    and the size of the white rabbit is small
    and the white rabbit carries the pocket watch
    and the white rabbit carries fan
    and the white rabbit carries gloves
    and the small door is in hall
    and the small door is closed
    and the small door is locked
    and the glass table is in hall
    and the golden key is on the glass table
    and bottle is in hall
    and cake is in hall
    and mouse is in the pool of tears.

% ---- the hole goes one way

it must not be true that
    a person goes up from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in hall at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person goes up from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in the rabbit hole at the first time.

% ---- the pool of tears, once it exists, is below the hall

down from hall leads to the pool of tears at a time if
    the pool of tears exists at the time.

% ---- size: the bottle, the cake, the fan

when a person drinks a thing
    and the size of the person is a size
then it is not the case that the size of the person is the size.

when a person drinks a thing
then the size of the person is small.

when a person drinks a thing
then it is not the case that the thing is in a holder.

when a person drinks a thing
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person eats a thing
    and the size of the person is a size
then it is not the case that the size of the person is the size.

when a person eats a thing
then the size of the person is huge.

when a person eats a thing
then it is not the case that the thing is in a holder.

when a person eats a thing
then it is not the case that the person carries the thing.

when a person waves a thing
    and the thing is a fan
    and the size of the person is a size
then it is not the case that the size of the person is the size.

when a person waves a thing
    and the thing is a fan
then the size of the person is small.

it must not be true that
    a person drinks a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is drinkable.

it must not be true that
    a person drinks a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person eats a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the thing is edible.

it must not be true that
    a person eats a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person can reach the thing at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person waves a thing from a first time to a second time
    and it is not the case that the person carries the thing at the first time.

% ---- the door is fifteen inches high, and the table is three feet

it must not be true that
    a person goes south from a first time to a second time
    and the person is in hall at the first time
    and it is not the case that the size of the person is small at the first time.

it must not be true that
    a person takes a thing from a first time to a second time
    and the thing is on the glass table at the first time
    and the size of the person is small at the first time.

% ---- a huge Alice who cannot get out cries a pool; a small one falls in

if the turn ends from a first time to a second time
    and the size of player is huge at the second time
    and player is in hall at the second time
    and it is not the case that player has cried at the second time
then player cries from the second time to a third time.

when a person cries
then the person has cried.

when a person cries
then the pool of tears exists.

if the turn ends from a first time to a second time
    and the size of player is small at the second time
    and player is in hall at the second time
    and the pool of tears exists at the second time
then player falls into the pool of tears from the second time to a third time.

when a person falls into a room
    and the person is in a place
then it is not the case that the person is in the place.

when a person falls into a room
then the person is in the room.

% ---- the White Rabbit: a route, one stop a turn, and a return for the fan

when a person runs from a room to a second room
then it is not the case that the person is in the room.

when a person runs from a room to a second room
then the person is in the second room.

if the turn ends from a first time to a second time
    and the white rabbit is in a room at the second time
    and the rabbit runs from the room to a second room
then the white rabbit runs from the room to the second room from the second time to a third time.

if the turn ends from a first time to a second time
    and the white rabbit is in garden at the second time
    and the pool of tears exists at the second time
    and the white rabbit carries fan at the second time
then the white rabbit runs from garden to hall from the second time to a third time.

if the white rabbit is in hall at a time
    and the pool of tears exists at the time
    and the white rabbit carries fan at the time
then the white rabbit drops fan from the time to a second time
    and the white rabbit drops gloves from the time to the second time.

% ---- chapters

if the first chapter is playing at a time
    and player is in hall at the time
then terminate the first chapter is playing from the time to a second time
    and initiate the first chapter has ended below from the time to the second time
    and initiate the second chapter is playing from the time to the second time.

if the second chapter is playing at a time
    and player is in the pool of tears at the time
then terminate the second chapter is playing from the time to a second time
    and initiate the second chapter has ended wet from the time to the second time.

if the second chapter is playing at a time
    and player is in garden at the time
then terminate the second chapter is playing from the time to a second time
    and initiate the second chapter has ended in the garden from the time to the second time.

% ---- the story's own commands: tries, never obligations

if the command is to drink a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to drink the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to eat a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to eat the thing from the second time to a third time.

if the command is to wave a thing from a first time to a second time
then player tries to wave the thing from the second time to a third time.

a person tries to drink a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person drinks the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to drink a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot drink the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to eat a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person eats the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to eat a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot eat the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to wave a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person waves the thing from the first time to the second time.

a person tries to wave a thing from a first time to a second time if
    the person cannot wave the thing from the first time to the second time.

